-- #3186: half-open `s.[lo..hi]` past the end of a String.  Until this fixture landed
-- the String arm of `Slice` CLAMPED — `"hello".[2..99]` printed `llo` and exited 0 on
-- BOTH engines, disagreeing with `s.[lo..hi]` being the panicking form (string.mdk's
-- `sliceClamped` doc) and with `Slice (Array a)`, which had panicked since #550.
main = println "hello".[2..99]
